  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 7, 'Iterative and agile approach'. Three circular loops sit along a horizontal timeline arrow: Minimum viable product (MVP), then VERSION 1, then VERSION 2. Each loop has the same four stages: understand and prioritize user requirements, design (adapt design in later versions), build and test, and train users. Milestones along the arrow read: determine that a PCPOSS is an appropriate health intervention; repeat the previous loop until meeting MVP specs to deploy; deploy and roll out; gather and manage user feedback; deploy and roll out; gather and manage user feedback; deploy, roll out and scale; and iterations for continuous improvement.",
